- Subject: Quick meeting — settlement vs trial questions (case in Maricopa County)
- Body: Hi Sarah — discovery just closed and I want to decide whether to accept a settlement or proceed to trial. Can we set a meeting or call? For that meeting I’d like your assessment of (1) our case strengths/weaknesses, (2) likely outcomes and award ranges, (3) estimated additional costs and timeline to trial, and (4) whether you recommend mediation or a counter-offer. I have the settlement offer and discovery documents ready. Suggested times: [two options]. Thanks — [Your name]
If you’d like, I can draft a more detailed list of points for you to sign off on or send directly to Sarah.

Final notes and offer to help
- Before making any final decision, get the specific numbers and probabilities from Sarah and confirm the court/venue.
- If you want, I can:
  - Draft a specific counteroffer or settlement term sheet for you to review (non‑filed draft).
  - Turn the question list into a printable checklist to take to your meeting.
  - Draft an email to Sarah using your voice and details of any settlement offer you already have.

