8) Red flags about a settlement you should question
- Vague or overly broad release language
- No security for payments (especially if respondent has a history of nonpayment)
- Attempts to require you to waive unrelated rights
- Deadline pressure to accept without time to consult or review
- Offer below clear documented losses without good counterweight (e.g., confidentiality)

