- Certainty vs risk: settlement gives certainty; trial has uncertainty but maybe a much better outcome
- Emotional toll: personal stress and time involved in trial preparation/testifying
- Enforceability: is the settlement easier to enforce than a court judgment? (Sometimes settlements include enforcement mechanisms)
- Precedent and principle: does letting the respondent “win” create an undesirable precedent for future issues?
